1.4 Representing Negative Numbers
Sign and Magnitude
• First bit = sign (0 = positive, 1 = negative)
• Example (8-bit):
+5 = 00000101
-5 = 10000101
❌ Problem: two zeros (00000000 and 10000000)
Two’s Complement (used in computers)
Steps:
• Write binary for positive number.
• Invert all bits.
• Add 1.
Example:
+5 = 00000101
Invert → 11111010
Add 1 → 11111011 = -5
Range for 8-bit: –128 to +127
1.5 Binary Shifts
Used for multiplying or dividing by powers of 2.
• Left shift by 1: ×2
• Right shift by 1: ÷2
1.6 Character Sets
Characters are stored as binary codes.
