⚙️ CHAPTER 3 – HARDWARE
3.1 Computer Components
Main hardware types:
• Input Devices: Keyboard, Mouse, Scanner, Microphone.
• Output Devices: Monitor, Printer, Speaker.
• Storage Devices: Hard Disk, SSD, Flash drive.
• Processing Device: CPU.
3.2 CPU (Central Processing Unit)
Main Components
• ALU (Arithmetic Logic Unit): Performs maths and logic operations.
• CU (Control Unit): Controls all operations using control signals.
• Registers: Small, fast memory inside CPU.
• PC (Program Counter): Holds address of next instruction.
• CIR (Current Instruction Register): Holds current instruction.
• MAR (Memory Address Register): Address of data to fetch/store.
• MDR (Memory Data Register): Actual data being transferred.
• Accumulator: Holds results from ALU.
Fetch–Decode–Execute Cycle
• Fetch: CU sends address from PC to memory, retrieves instruction.
• Decode: CU interprets instruction.
• Execute: ALU carries out operation.
• PC updated to next instruction.
